 ### [Level 1 Triangle-Voxel Classification](4872-level-1-triangle-voxel-classification.md)
-Level 1 Triangle-Voxel Classification is a coarse-grained method for mapping mesh triangles to a 3D voxel grid by determining which voxels overlap with each triangle's bounding volume. It serves as the initial stage in hierarchical voxelization, significantly reducing the search space for subsequent fine-grained classification steps. Unlike brute-force approaches that test every voxel against every triangle, this method uses vertex mapping to identify candidate voxels, processing one triangle per thread for parallel efficiency.
+Classifies input triangles into a coarse 3D voxel grid by mapping vertices to voxel indices and testing overlap with all candidate voxels the triangle spans. It identifies candidate voxels via vertex mapping rather than testing every voxel against every triangle, enabling parallel processing where each thread handles one triangle.
 
 ### [Tessellation-based Voxelization](5430-tessellation-based-voxelization.md)
-Tessellation-based Voxelization is a GPU-accelerated method for generating 3D voxel grids from triangle meshes by leveraging the hardware tessellation pipeline to subdivide geometry before rasterization. It differs from fixed-function or CPU-based voxelizers by enabling adaptive triangle density and displacement mapping during the generation phase, allowing for higher fidelity in complex regions.
